    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0541" n="1275" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1275"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mavroyeni Bey to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Legation of Turkey</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    confirm my note of yesterday’s date relative to the Tarsus incident.</p>
                <p>Owing to an error in the transmission of the Sublime Porte’s telegram, I told
                    your excellency that the quarrel had taken place between a cook named Christi,
                    who was the bearer of American papers, and a certain Zeibek Ali. I should have
                    said, “The quarrel took place between the cook of Mr. Christie, an American
                    citizen, and a certain Zéibek Ali.”</p>
                <p>I beg your excellency to take note of this correction.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mavroyeni.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
